+// node-turn forwards peer→client ChannelData (allocation.js) but DROPS the
+// reverse direction: message.read() rejects any frame whose top 2 bits aren't
+// zero, and a ChannelData channel number (0x4000–0x7FFE) has bit 1 set. So a
+// client that channel-binds and sends media as ChannelData never gets relayed.
+// This mirrors the send.js Send-indication path: look up the allocation for the
+// source 5-tuple, resolve the bound peer for the frame's channel number, and
+// send the inner data out the allocation's relay socket to that peer.
